<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edward the Black Prince</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1330–1376</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Edward of Woodstock, Black Prince</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edward the Black Prince (Edward of Woodstock) was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III of England</a> and a celebrated commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>. He fought at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-crecy">Crécy</a> in 1346, captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-ii-of-france">John II of France</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a> in 1356 and ruled Aquitaine as its prince from 1362. His victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najera">Nájera</a> in 1367 was followed by heavy taxes, revolt and illness, and he died a year before his father; his son became Richard II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edward-the-black-prince.jpg" alt="Edward the Black Prince" width="320" height="358" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Josep Renalias · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TombaPrincepNegre_(cropped).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
